name toxigen-generations
# The generations, written out from Parquet as a table whose first row names its columns. Of a generation the row says
# its prompt, how it was generated and the classifier's prediction; of the prompt, its label and group. Each said
# together.
# The card's "Data Fields":
#   "**prompt** is the prompt used for **generation**."
#   "**generation** is the TOXIGEN generated text."
#   "**generation_method** denotes whether or not ALICE was used to generate the corresponding generation. If this
#   value is ALICE, then ALICE was used, if it is TopK, then ALICE was not used."
#   "**prompt_label** is the binary value indicating whether or not the prompt is toxic (1 is toxic, 0 is benign)."
#   "**group** indicates the target group of the prompt."
#   "**roberta_prediction** is the probability predicted by our corresponding RoBERTa model for each instance."
match train/train-*.tsv

tier row by \n
header
escaped \
tier field by \t

thing row generation
content *
together row
value - generation_method
relation "the prompt used for generation" prompt
relation "the probability predicted by our corresponding RoBERTa model" roberta_prediction
relation "whether or not the prompt is toxic" prompt_label
relation "the target group of the prompt" group
attest row prompt generation_method roberta_prediction
attest row prompt_label group of prompt
